Material used at build or test time, and NOT distributed with this program
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Ghostty / libghostty-vt (MIT)
    The differential test harness builds and links the real libghostty-vt and compares
    this project's terminal grid against it, case by case. It is depended on by exactly
    one crate, `difftest`, and it is not part of the shipped artifact: the app binary
    contains zero Ghostty symbols and links zero Ghostty libraries.

    No Ghostty source is copied into this repository. Parts of the terminal core's
    BEHAVIOUR were derived by reading Ghostty's source to establish why the reference
    library does what it does. Black-box probing establishes what differs; the source
    explains why. That is derivation of behaviour from a published reference, not
    transcription of it, and agreement is measured through the ABI boundary rather than
    assumed from shared code.

    https://ghostty.org

Miriam Mono CLM (GPL-2.0), by Maxim Iorsh, from the Culmus project, culmus-0.140,
    unmodified. It was the shipped Hebrew face until 2026-08-25 and is now a TEST FIXTURE
    only, at crates/render/tests/fixtures/, kept because it is the only face measured here
    whose unshaped path visibly misplaces a niqqud mark -- which is what lets the GPOS
    control in tests/shaping.rs go red. scripts/build-app.sh copies assets/fonts/*.ttf and
    never looks in that directory, so it is not distributed with this program.
    LICENSE-Culmus-GPL2.txt travels with it.
    https://culmus.sourceforge.io

esctest2 (GPL-2.0)
    A terminal conformance suite, vendored on demand by scripts/fetch-esctest.sh and run
    against this project's own pty at test time only. Pinned in esctest.lock. Not
    distributed with this program.
    https://github.com/ThomasDickey/esctest2

Unicode Character Database (Unicode License)
    BidiTest.txt and BidiCharacterTest.txt, vendored on demand by scripts/fetch-ucd.sh and
    used as the conformance oracle for bidirectional reordering. Pinned in ucd.lock. Not
    distributed with this program.
    https://www.unicode.org/Public/UCD/

